        "contact": {
          "name": "State of Colorado",
          "url": "https://data.colorado.gov"
        },
        "description": "Explore a wide range of public datasets and resources from the Colorado Information Marketplace, including information on government revenue and expenditures, transportation, demographics, business, and more. Access charts, maps, datasets, and documents to gain insights into various aspects of life in Colorado. A valuable tool for researchers, businesses, and the general public seeking data-driven insights.",
        "servers": [
          {
            "description": "Colorado Information Marketplace API",
            "url": "https://data.colorado.gov/api"
          }
        ],
        "termsOfService": "https://colorado.gov/terms-of-use",
        "title": "Colorado Information Marketplace",
        "version": "1.0.0",
        "tagline": "Browse the State of Colorado's open data portal covering business, transportation, demographics, water, energy, health and more",
        "homepage": "https://data.colorado.gov/",
        "docs_url": "https://data.colorado.gov/browse",
        "license_short": "State of Colorado open data; check each dataset's terms of use",
        "license_md": "- Data is published by the State of Colorado as part of its open data programme; see the portal's [Terms of Use](https://data.colorado.gov/) for general conditions.\n- Each dataset may carry its own licence, attribution requirement or refresh schedule, so check the dataset metadata before redistribution.\n- The portal is powered by the Socrata Open Data platform (Tyler Technologies); the Socrata Open Data API (SODA) conventions apply to all `resource/{id}` endpoints.",
        "about_md": "The [Colorado Information Marketplace](https://data.colorado.gov/) is the [State of Colorado](https://data.colorado.gov/)'s open data portal, run on the Socrata Open Data platform (Tyler Technologies). It exposes hundreds of state government datasets so the public can query, chart and reuse them.\n\nDatasets are grouped into eleven public categories on the portal:\n\n- Water\n- Business\n- Demographics\n- Transportation\n- Energy\n- Early Childhood\n- Recreation\n- Health\n- Education\n- Public Safety\n- Agriculture\n\nEach dataset is published as a Socrata resource and is reachable as JSON via `https://data.colorado.gov/resource/{dataset-id}.json` (for example `resource/4ykn-tg5h.json` for Colorado business entities). Standard SODA query parameters such as `$where`, `$select`, `$limit` and `$offset` are supported on these resource endpoints.\n\nAccess is open and CORS is enabled, so the API can be called directly from browser code; high-volume users are encouraged to register a Socrata application token to lift throttling on shared, anonymous traffic.",
        "entity_desc": {
          "catalog": "The portal's dataset catalog — individual datasets are addressed as Socrata resources at `https://data.colorado.gov/resource/{dataset-id}.json` and span business, transportation, demographics, water, energy, health, education, public safety, agriculture, recreation and early childhood."
        },
